{
  "summary": "Validates the `-signetchallenge` command-line argument in `bitcoin-cli` using the same hex-parsing logic as `bitcoind`. It introduces a shared `ReadSigNetChallengeArg()` helper called during signet argument and directory processing, producing an explicit hex parse error on invalid input.",
  "problem": "When a user passes invalid hex to `-signetchallenge` in `bitcoin-cli`, the client does not report an invalid hex error; instead, it fails later with an authorization/cookie error because it looks in the wrong directory, leaving the user with an ambiguous diagnostic message.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: Demonstrates that `bitcoind -signet -signetchallenge=z` returns `Error: -signetchallenge must be hex, not 'z'`, whereas `bitcoin-cli -signet -signetchallenge=z` silently fails auth with `error: Authorization failed: ... Is your -signetchallenge correct for custom signets?`",
    "PR description: Notes it addresses a review comment from PR #34566."
  ],
